{
  "_doc": [
    "Shared linkify vectors: ONE contract for both import sides.",
    "Server: api/services/journal_two/note_connectors/convert/linkify.py (test_linkify.py reads this file).",
    "Client: Plan B linkPolicy.js linkifyTextNodes (its test reads this file too), so the two cannot drift.",
    "Each vector: `text` placed in `context`; `links` = the links linkify CREATES, in order, as {text, href}.",
    "context: plain = a paragraph text run; inline_code = a run with a code mark (<code>);",
    "code_block = a codeBlock (<pre>); link = a run already inside a link (<a href=\"https://existing.example/\">);",
    "inline_math / block_math = math nodes (data-type inline-math / block-math). Every non-plain context must come out untouched.",
    "Rule (linkify-it 5 defaults, the same instance markdown-it uses): keep a match only when its schema is http:, https: or",
    "mailto: (a bare email counts; href gets mailto:), or its schema is empty and its raw text starts with www. (case-insensitive;",
    "href gets https://). Every other fuzzy domain (NVDA.US, example.com), ftp: and // is dropped.",
    "Then ONE trim, the same on both sides: cut the match at the first character of",
    "U+3000 U+3001 U+3002 U+FF0C U+FF1B U+FF1A U+FF01 U+FF1F U+FF08 U+FF09 U+3010 U+3011 U+300C U+300D U+300E U+300F U+300A U+300B",
    "U+3008 U+3009 U+201C U+201D U+2018 U+2019 U+2026 (CJK/fullwidth punctuation and curly quotes, which linkify-it keeps inside a",
    "path), then strip trailing . , : ; ! ? characters; then keep the result only if linkify-it matches it again as exactly one",
    "kept link spanning the whole trimmed text."
  ],
  "version": 1,
  "vectors": [
    {"name": "http", "context": "plain", "text": "see http://example.com/a now",
     "links": [{"text": "http://example.com/a", "href": "http://example.com/a"}]},
    {"name": "https with query, trailing comma", "context": "plain", "text": "See https://finviz.com/quote.ashx?t=NVDA, ok",
     "links": [{"text": "https://finviz.com/quote.ashx?t=NVDA", "href": "https://finviz.com/quote.ashx?t=NVDA"}]},
    {"name": "www, trailing period, href gets https", "context": "plain", "text": "see www.tradingview.com/x.",
     "links": [{"text": "www.tradingview.com/x", "href": "https://www.tradingview.com/x"}]},
    {"name": "explicit mailto", "context": "plain", "text": "mail mailto:me@x.com today",
     "links": [{"text": "mailto:me@x.com", "href": "mailto:me@x.com"}]},
    {"name": "bare email, trailing period", "context": "plain", "text": "write a@b.com.",
     "links": [{"text": "a@b.com", "href": "mailto:a@b.com"}]},
    {"name": "three kinds in one run", "context": "plain", "text": "see https://example.com/x?y=1 and www.example.org or a@b.com",
     "links": [{"text": "https://example.com/x?y=1", "href": "https://example.com/x?y=1"},
               {"text": "www.example.org", "href": "https://www.example.org"},
               {"text": "a@b.com", "href": "mailto:a@b.com"}]},
    {"name": "wrapping parentheses and trailing period", "context": "plain", "text": "(see https://x.com/a).",
     "links": [{"text": "https://x.com/a", "href": "https://x.com/a"}]},
    {"name": "balanced parentheses in a Wikipedia URL", "context": "plain",
     "text": "(https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bracket_(disambiguation))",
     "links": [{"text": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bracket_(disambiguation)",
                "href": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bracket_(disambiguation)"}]},
    {"name": "trailing question mark", "context": "plain", "text": "is it https://x.com/b?",
     "links": [{"text": "https://x.com/b", "href": "https://x.com/b"}]},
    {"name": "trailing exclamation mark", "context": "plain", "text": "wow https://x.com/a!",
     "links": [{"text": "https://x.com/a", "href": "https://x.com/a"}]},
    {"name": "trailing colon", "context": "plain", "text": "see https://x.com/a: next",
     "links": [{"text": "https://x.com/a", "href": "https://x.com/a"}]},
    {"name": "a port is not a trailing colon", "context": "plain", "text": "at https://x.com:8080/b today",
     "links": [{"text": "https://x.com:8080/b", "href": "https://x.com:8080/b"}]},
    {"name": "trailing semicolon", "context": "plain", "text": "https://x.com/a; b",
     "links": [{"text": "https://x.com/a", "href": "https://x.com/a"}]},
    {"name": "Chinese full stop ends a URL", "context": "plain", "text": "见 https://example.com/路径。好",
     "links": [{"text": "https://example.com/路径", "href": "https://example.com/路径"}]},
    {"name": "fullwidth comma ends a URL", "context": "plain", "text": "see https://example.com/a，then",
     "links": [{"text": "https://example.com/a", "href": "https://example.com/a"}]},
    {"name": "period then Chinese full stop", "context": "plain", "text": "https://x.com/a.。",
     "links": [{"text": "https://x.com/a", "href": "https://x.com/a"}]},
    {"name": "www after a space, Chinese full stop", "context": "plain", "text": "参考 www.example.com。",
     "links": [{"text": "www.example.com", "href": "https://www.example.com"}]},
    {"name": "www glued to CJK text is not a www match (Plan B rule)", "context": "plain", "text": "参考www.example.com。",
     "links": []},
    {"name": "curly quotes around a URL", "context": "plain", "text": "see “https://x.com/a” here",
     "links": [{"text": "https://x.com/a", "href": "https://x.com/a"}]},
    {"name": "IDN hosts", "context": "plain", "text": "https://münchen.de/x and www.bücher.de.",
     "links": [{"text": "https://münchen.de/x", "href": "https://münchen.de/x"},
               {"text": "www.bücher.de", "href": "https://www.bücher.de"}]},
    {"name": "upper-case scheme and www", "context": "plain", "text": "HTTPS://X.COM/A WWW.X.COM",
     "links": [{"text": "HTTPS://X.COM/A", "href": "HTTPS://X.COM/A"},
               {"text": "WWW.X.COM", "href": "https://WWW.X.COM"}]},
    {"name": "query and fragment kept, trailing period dropped", "context": "plain", "text": "www.x.com/a?q=1&r=2#frag.",
     "links": [{"text": "www.x.com/a?q=1&r=2#frag", "href": "https://www.x.com/a?q=1&r=2#frag"}]},
    {"name": "ticker with a country suffix", "context": "plain", "text": "long NVDA.US into earnings", "links": []},
    {"name": "dollar ticker with a country suffix", "context": "plain", "text": "$NVDA.US", "links": []},
    {"name": "bare domain", "context": "plain", "text": "see example.com today", "links": []},
    {"name": "class share ticker", "context": "plain", "text": "BRK.B held", "links": []},
    {"name": "version number", "context": "plain", "text": "v2.3 shipped", "links": []},
    {"name": "ftp scheme", "context": "plain", "text": "ftp://x.org", "links": []},
    {"name": "protocol-relative", "context": "plain", "text": "//cdn.example.com/x.jpg", "links": []},
    {"name": "scheme with nothing after it", "context": "plain", "text": "x https://", "links": []},
    {"name": "URL in inline code", "context": "inline_code", "text": "https://a.com", "links": []},
    {"name": "URL in a code block", "context": "code_block", "text": "curl https://b.com/api", "links": []},
    {"name": "URL inside an existing link", "context": "link", "text": "https://e.com", "links": []},
    {"name": "URL inside inline math", "context": "inline_math", "text": "https://c.com", "links": []},
    {"name": "URL inside block math", "context": "block_math", "text": "https://d.com", "links": []}
  ]
}
